WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:13.745
The Lost Boys were walking through the woods.

2
00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:19.388
They were hoping to greet their captain, Peter Pan, after his trip to the nursery.

3
00:00:20.268 --> 00:00:25.410
But while the Lost Boys were looking for Peter, the pirates were looking for the Lost Boys.

4
00:00:26.431 --> 00:00:28.992
Meanwhile, the Indians were looking for the pirates.

5
00:00:30.528 --> 00:00:32.829
And the wild animals were looking for the Indians.

6
00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.590
It was like a grand march.

7
00:00:36.611 --> 00:00:40.092
Everyone was going round and round the island, ready to fight if they met.

8
00:00:41.072 --> 00:00:45.254
But they did not meet because they were all walking at the same speed!

9
00:00:46.255 --> 00:00:49.356
The Lost Boys were dressed in bear skins and had their daggers ready.

10
00:00:50.476 --> 00:00:53.197
There were six of them, and they were all very sweet.

11
00:00:54.678 --> 00:00:56.199
But they could be wild at times.

12
00:00:56.879 --> 00:00:59.200
Of course, they were all very young.

13
00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.283
Whenever one of them began to grow up, Peter quickly sent that boy away.

14
00:01:05.324 --> 00:01:07.466
It was against the rules to grow up in Neverland.

15
00:01:08.507 --> 00:01:11.949
As the march continued, each boy was firmly on the lookout.

16
00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:14.151
Tootles was brave.

17
00:01:15.072 --> 00:01:17.954
But he always seemed to miss the fighting when a battle broke out.

18
00:01:18.955 --> 00:01:24.499
Adventures would always happen just when he stepped around a corner to gather a few sticks of firewood.

19
00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.024
When he'd return, the other boys would be covered in blood and the enemy would be gone.

20
00:01:30.988 --> 00:01:32.649
He was the easiest boy to trick.

21
00:01:33.969 --> 00:01:36.730
Everyone knew this—including Tinker Bell.

22
00:01:37.691 --> 00:01:41.392
Handsome Nibs was followed by Slightly, the boldest boy of the group.

23
00:01:41.412 --> 00:01:46.474
"I am the only one not afraid of pirates," Slightly boasted.

24
00:01:47.395 --> 00:01:48.875
But no one ever believed him.

25
00:01:50.436 --> 00:01:56.719
Curly, who always got into trouble for something— even when he hadn't done it, was the fourth in

26
00:01:56.759 --> 00:01:59.660
line. And last were the twins.

27
00:02:00.704 --> 00:02:04.006
They looked so much alike that even Peter couldn't tell one from the other.

28
00:02:05.007 --> 00:02:06.487
The twins didn't talk much.

29
00:02:07.748 --> 00:02:11.791
The pirates followed right behind the Lost Boys—right in their footsteps!

30
00:02:12.951 --> 00:02:16.894
As the pirates walked through the trees, they bragged about their latest adventures.

31
00:02:17.854 --> 00:02:20.656
The men were laughing and singing loud pirate songs.

32
00:02:21.736 --> 00:02:24.278
Huge and handsome Cecco wore coins in his ears.

33
00:02:25.459 --> 00:02:27.720
Bill Jukes had tattoos all over his body.

34
00:02:28.992 --> 00:02:31.414
Cookson was said to be the son of a famous pirate.

35
00:02:32.255 --> 00:02:35.758
Bloodthirsty Gentleman Starkey once worked in a public school.

36
00:02:36.799 --> 00:02:41.903
The bandits Skylights, Robert Mullins, and Alf Mason also belonged to the pirate crew.

37
00:02:43.144 --> 00:02:45.326
All three of them were famous on the high seas.

38
00:02:46.427 --> 00:02:49.689
Pirate Noodler had hands that looked as if they were on backwards.

39
00:02:51.311 --> 00:02:53.272
Finally, there was friendly Smee.

40
00:02:54.533 --> 00:02:57.476
His job was to look after the pirate ship and Captain Hook.

41
00:02:58.536 --> 00:03:03.878
In front of the line, sitting in a chariot pulled by his men, was Captain James Hook.

42
00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.459
He yelled orders at his men as if they were dogs.

43
00:03:08.499 --> 00:03:12.400
Hook was handsome, with long black curls and deep blue eyes.

44
00:03:14.001 --> 00:03:16.721
In fact, the man was very fashionable.

45
00:03:17.942 --> 00:03:20.902
He wore a starched lace collar under his splendid red jacket.

46
00:03:22.043 --> 00:03:25.844
His tall black boots shone because Smee polished them every day.

47
00:03:27.084 --> 00:03:29.806
The captain always had a cigar hanging from his lip.

48
00:03:30.966 --> 00:03:33.287
The Indians followed the boot marks of the pirates.

49
00:03:34.388 --> 00:03:37.310
They moved silently down the path carrying their tomahawks.

50
00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.511
Their bodies were shiny with paint and oil.

51
00:03:41.712 --> 00:03:45.094
Braided around their necks was the hair of pirates they had killed.

52
00:03:46.314 --> 00:03:48.015
The Indians didn't say one word.

53
00:03:49.876 --> 00:03:53.078
Great Big Little Panther crept quietly on his hands and knees.

54
00:03:54.119 --> 00:03:56.320
Princess Tiger Lily walked proudly upright.

55
00:03:57.512 --> 00:04:04.617
Next in the line of characters came the wild animals—lions, tigers, bears, and other beasts.

56
00:04:05.718 --> 00:04:07.519
Their tongues were hanging out with hunger.

57
00:04:10.961 --> 00:04:12.262
The animals were ready.

58
00:04:13.423 --> 00:04:18.206
They might catch a boy, a pirate, an Indian, or even one of their own.

59
00:04:19.307 --> 00:04:22.289
The last in line was a giant crocodile.

60
00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:26.552
He was looking for one victim only—Captain Hook.

61
00:04:28.364 --> 00:04:31.666
The march might have gone on forever, but one of the groups stopped.

62
00:04:33.127 --> 00:04:34.428
It was the Lost Boys.

63
00:04:34.949 --> 00:04:36.670
They heard pirate laughter in the distance.

64
00:04:37.871 --> 00:04:39.932
And they heard a scary pirate song.

65
00:04:40.352 --> 00:04:44.315
"Yo ho!

66
00:04:44.375 --> 00:04:45.436
Yo ho!

67
00:04:45.496 --> 00:04:47.757
The pirate life!

68
00:04:47.797 --> 00:04:49.979
The skull and bones!

69
00:04:50.259 --> 00:04:54.042
Hey, hey, they'll go down to Davy Jones!"

70
00:04:54.062 --> 00:04:57.004
"Davy Jones!"

71
00:04:57.732 --> 00:04:58.474
thought the boys.

72
00:04:59.515 --> 00:05:01.238
That meant the bottom of the ocean!

73
00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.384
The boys ran swiftly through the woods.

74
00:05:05.346 --> 00:05:08.691
They were quick as bunnies, returning to their home under the ground.
